
🗣️ Active Voice और Passive Voice क्या है?

Active Voice: जब कर्ता (subject) स्वयं कार्य करता है।
➤ Ram eats an apple.

Passive Voice: जब कार्य किसी अन्य द्वारा किया जाता है और वाक्य में कर्म (object) को पहले रखा जाता है।
➤ An apple is eaten by Ram.



---

📚 Voice बदलने के नियम (General Rules to Change Voice)

Element	Active	Passive

Subject	करता	कर्म बन जाता है
Object	कर्म	कर्ता बन जाता है
Verb	Tense के अनुसार बदला जाता है	"Be + V3" का प्रयोग होता है
Helping Verb	Tense के अनुसार बदला जाता है	“is/am/are, was/were, be, been, being, will be, etc.”
By	Passive voice में agent के पहले ‘by’ लगता है	



---

🔄 All Tense-wise Active to Passive Rules

✅ 1. Simple Present

🔹 Rule: is/am/are + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: She writes a letter.

Passive: A letter is written by her.



---

✅ 2. Present Continuous

🔹 Rule: is/am/are + being + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: He is reading a book.

Passive: A book is being read by him.



---

✅ 3. Present Perfect

🔹 Rule: has/have + been + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: They have completed the work.

Passive: The work has been completed by them.



---

✅ 4. Simple Past

🔹 Rule: was/were + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: She cooked food.

Passive: Food was cooked by her.



---

✅ 5. Past Continuous

🔹 Rule: was/were + being + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: He was writing a letter.

Passive: A letter was being written by him.



---

✅ 6. Past Perfect

🔹 Rule: had + been + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: They had finished the task.

Passive: The task had been finished by them.



---

✅ 7. Simple Future

🔹 Rule: will/shall + be + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: He will complete the work.

Passive: The work will be completed by him.



---

✅ 8. Future Perfect

🔹 Rule: will/shall + have + been + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: She will have written the book.

Passive: The book will have been written by her.



---

🚫 Note:

✖️ Future Continuous, Present Perfect Continuous, Past Perfect Continuous, Future Perfect Continuous – इन Tense का Passive voice नहीं बनता।


---

✍️ Modals (Can, May, Must, Should...)

🔹 Rule: Modal + be + V3
🔹 Example:

Active: She can drive a car.

Passive: A car can be driven by her.



---

💬 Imperative Sentences (आदेश, निवेदन, सुझाव)

Sentence Type	Structure

Positive Command:	Let + object + be + V3<br>e.g., Close the door. → Let the door be closed.
Negative Command:	Let + object + not + be + V3<br>e.g., Do not waste time. → Let time not be wasted.
Request:	You are requested to + V1<br>e.g., Please help me. → You are requested to help me.



---

📘 Pronoun Changes (Subject ⇄ Object)

Subject (Active)	Object (Passive)

I	me
We	us
You	you
He	him
She	her
They	them
It	it



